course: dictionary
lesson: 12443
title: Decompose: rot, split, or break down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To decompose means to break down into smaller parts. Most often it means something dead slowly rotting away. «Dead leaves decompose on the forest floor over many months.» Tiny creatures and fungi do the work, and the leaves slowly turn into soil.
explain: In science, decompose can also mean a substance breaking into simpler parts. In maths, it means splitting a number into smaller parts to make working easier. «To multiply 36 by 4, decompose 36 into 30 and 6.» Context tells you which meaning you need: look for the words around it, such as leaves, chemicals or numbers.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Dead leaves break down slowly on the forest floor» still makes sense, so decompose is the right meaning.
fact: To decompose means to rot or break down slowly.
fact: Decomposers such as worms, fungi and bacteria make dead things decompose into soil.
fact: A compost heap works because food scraps and leaves decompose there.
fact: In science, «decompose» can mean breaking a substance into simpler parts or chemicals.
fact: In maths, «decompose a number» means splitting it into smaller parts, such as 47 = 40 + 7.
exercise: «Dead leaves slowly decompose on the forest floor.» What does decompose mean here? | To shine brightly at night | To grow very tall quickly | *To rot and break down slowly | To freeze solid in winter
exercise: In maths, what does it mean to decompose 47? | Multiply it by 7 | Write it out in words | *Split it into 40 and 7 | Round it up to 50
exercise: Which helpers make dead things decompose in a compost heap? | Lorries and bicycles | *Worms and fungi | Pencils and rulers | Sunshine and wind alone
test: «Scientists can decompose a substance into simpler parts.» In science, what does decompose mean? | To weigh a substance very carefully | To paint a substance a new colour | To make a substance freeze solid | *To break a substance into simpler parts
test: Which is a correct way to decompose 36 × 4? | *30 × 4 + 6 × 4 | 36 + 4 | 30 + 6 + 4 | 3 × 6 × 4
exam: «The old log was fully decomposed and crumbled into soil.» What does fully decomposed most likely mean? | *Completely rotted away into soil | Painted bright red | Lifted high into the air | Freshly cut and still green
